<!--
  Status-bar notification icon.

  MUST be a flat silhouette with a real alpha channel. Since Android 5 the system
  redraws the notification icon using only its alpha, filling every opaque pixel
  with one colour — so a full-colour launcher icon (which is what Android falls
  back to when no default_notification_icon is declared) arrives as a solid white
  blob. That is the white-square symptom, and it is a resource problem, not a
  delivery problem: the push itself was always being received.

  Kept in native/android/ because android/ is gitignored and fully regenerated by
  `npx cap add android`, exactly like native/android/google-services.json.
  scripts/patch-android-manifest.mjs copies it back in.
-->
